============================================================
SECTION 14 — TESTING AND VERIFICATION
============================================================

Testing must accompany implementation.

Use appropriate available checks:

- Unit tests.
- Integration tests.
- API contract tests.
- Static analysis.
- Dependency checks.
- Security checks.
- UI tests.
- Regression tests.
- Build verification.
- Runtime checks.
- Physical-device checks when required and available.

For every check, record the command or procedure and
the actual observed result.

Use these statuses precisely:

PASS:
The specified check executed and passed.

PARTIAL:
Some criteria passed, but the capability remains incomplete.

FAIL:
The check executed and failed, or a required criterion
was demonstrably not met.

BLOCKED:
A prerequisite prevented the check from running.

UNKNOWN:
Available evidence is insufficient.

NOT_TESTED:
The capability has not been tested.

NOT_VERIFIED_ON_DEVICE:
The feature has not been verified on the target device.

Do not change statuses without new evidence.

Do not suppress failing tests merely to obtain a green report.

Do not modify test expectations to hide an implementation defect.

